course: dictionary
lesson: 619
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words come from other languages, and they are not English words. «Baba» comes from Ukrainian and means grandmother or granny. In «Every Sunday, Taras in Leeds video calls his baba and dido (Ukrainian for gran and grandad) in Ukraine», the brackets tell you that baba is gran.
explain: The same spelling can mean different things, so check the clues. «Baba walks the phone round her garden to show him the tomatoes» shows a grown-up who shares her home life with family far away, so Baba here is a grandmother. Always ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Words also carry feelings. «BAbusya is a loving word for granny; BAba alone about a strange woman can sound rude.» Say «babusia» as BAH-boo-syah when you mean a loved grandmother. Say «baba» with care, because it can sound rude when used about a stranger.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Baba» is a Ukrainian word that means grandmother or granny.
fact: «Babusia» is a loving word for granny.
fact: A rum baba is a small sweet sponge cake soaked in syrup or rum.
fact: Baba Yaga is a witch in Slavic fairy tales who lives in a hut on chicken legs.
exercise: «Every Sunday, Taras in Leeds video calls his baba and dido (Ukrainian for gran and grandad) in Ukraine.» What does baba mean here? | A baby's bottle | A small sweet cake | A witch from a fairy tale | *Grandmother or granny
exercise: Who is Baba Yaga? | A Polish pudding made with apples | *A witch in Slavic fairy tales who lives in a hut on chicken legs | A famous English queen | A baker who sells sponge cakes
exercise: «A rum baba is a small sweet sponge cake soaked in syrup or rum.» What kind of thing is a rum baba? | *A cake | A witch | A baby | A grandmother
test: Which word means a loving way to say granny? | Dido | *Babusia | Rum | Baba Yaga
test: Why should you be careful about calling a stranger «baba»? | It means a fairy-tale witch, so it is always scary | It is a cake name, so it is silly | It is the Ukrainian word for a baby | *It can sound rude, because it is a word for a grandmother
exam: In baby talk, what can «baba» mean? | A tomato | A witch | A sponge cake soaked in rum | *A baby or a bottle
